  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Examining livestock depredation by tiger and its impact on farmers livelihood in Bhutans Jigme Dorji National Park</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human-wildlife conflict in Jigme Dorji National Park (JDNP), Bhutan, is costing farmers additional expenses, and possible personal injury. This project aims to examine the extent and magnitude of conflict between tiger and agro-pastoralists and propose a measure that may reduce the conflicts. The project will also conduct awareness programs on significance of conserving tiger in forest ecosystem in the park and neighboring regions. Project objectives include the following: (1) Examining livestock depredation by tiger and assessing its impact on farmer&apos;s livelihood; (2) Evaluating peoples perceptions and attitudes towards conservation of tigers; (3) Raising the awareness of the role of the tiger in forest ecosystem amongst inhabitants of JDNP through education programs and the distribution of educational materials; and, (4) Groundwork is laid for establishing an effective network of citizens to monitor and protect tiger, their prey species, and habitat amongst farmers in the lowland areas of JDNP.</narrative>
  </description>
